WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.022
Welcome to Free Study Bible.

2
00:00:03.522 --> 00:00:08.333
This short tour shows a free place to read, search, and study the Bible.

3
00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:15.938
Free Study Bible is free, non-commercial, and has no ads.

4
00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:26.231
The welcome page shows what is on it: Bibles, classic commentaries, daily devotionals, other Christian books, Christian media, and maps.

5
00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:29.589
Each card has buttons to read or to search.

6
00:00:30.103 --> 00:00:36.319
The menu on the left takes you to every part of the site. Click a group to open it, and see its pages.

7
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:41.313
Let's start with the Bible reader.

8
00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:45.876
Choose a Bible, a book, and a chapter, and press Go.

9
00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:54.683
Then just keep scrolling, to read on from chapter to chapter.

10
00:00:55.201 --> 00:01:06.487
Click a verse number for more about that verse: Show in Context, Other Translations, Related Verses, the original words, the commentaries, and your own notes.

11
00:01:06.995 --> 00:01:15.324
In the Berean Standard Bible, you can also click a word, to see the Hebrew or Greek word behind it, and every verse that uses it.

12
00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.733
You can also listen.

13
00:01:20.266 --> 00:01:25.281
Press Listen beside a chapter's name, or choose Listen from here on a verse.

14
00:01:25.786 --> 00:01:31.546
The verse being read is highlighted, and the reading carries on into the next chapter by itself.

15
00:01:34.788 --> 00:01:39.191
A bar at the foot lets you pause or stop, and choose the voice and the speed.

16
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:52.184
Search the Bible for words, an exact phrase, or a Strong's number.

17
00:01:52.691 --> 00:01:55.660
Here we search for, love one another.

18
00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:10.942
Every result has links: to the verse in context, the full chapter, other translations, related verses, and Download Card, which saves the verse as a picture to share.

19
00:02:11.478 --> 00:02:22.570
The list under the search box matches all the words, any word, or the exact phrase, and Search Options lets you search one Bible or several, and keep to part of the Bible.

20
00:02:23.106 --> 00:02:26.214
The results can also be filtered by book.

21
00:02:28.953 --> 00:02:38.663
Search Everything looks through the Bible, the commentaries, the devotionals, the other books, the media, the maps, and the FAQ, all at once.

22
00:02:39.173 --> 00:02:45.400
A search for grace finds the verses first, then what the commentators wrote, and the rest.

23
00:02:50.454 --> 00:03:00.861
The commentaries include classic works by Matthew Henry, John Gill, Adam Clarke, John Calvin, Martin Luther, Spurgeon, and more.

24
00:03:01.377 --> 00:03:04.253
Pick a book and a chapter, and press Read.

25
00:03:08.029 --> 00:03:11.528
Every Scripture reference in a note is a link to the verse.

26
00:03:15.252 --> 00:03:23.209
You can also search the commentaries, to find what the great teachers wrote about a word or a phrase, such as, born again.

27
00:03:29.053 --> 00:03:31.958
The devotionals open at today's date.

28
00:03:33.432 --> 00:03:39.161
Here is Daily Light on the Daily Path, with a reading for every morning and evening of the year.

29
00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:52.216
Other books brings classic Christian writing, from Augustine and Aquinas to Chesterton, Bunyan, Wesley, and Tozer, to read a chapter at a time.

30
00:03:52.744 --> 00:03:54.908
And you can search them, too.

31
00:04:01.586 --> 00:04:06.896
In the Apostles' Creed, every statement links to the Bible verse it comes from.

32
00:04:07.405 --> 00:04:10.080
Rest the pointer on one to see which.

33
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:18.459
Christian media has hymns, songs, and talks to listen to, each with its words.

34
00:04:18.972 --> 00:04:20.963
Open a song to play it.

35
00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:31.594
And you can search the media, by title, author, or the words of a song.

36
00:04:35.218 --> 00:04:38.212
Maps shows the lands and journeys of the Bible.

37
00:04:38.717 --> 00:04:44.121
Open a map, then drag it to move about, and zoom in to read the smallest towns.

38
00:04:51.649 --> 00:04:56.553
Under each map are the verses it goes with. Click one to read it in the Bible.

39
00:04:58.095 --> 00:05:03.304
Search the maps by a word, or by a verse, to find the maps that go with it.

40
00:05:07.018 --> 00:05:11.655
Every search page has one more choice: Search the Internet Archive.

41
00:05:15.579 --> 00:05:22.898
It searches inside millions of books and documents on archive.org, including its lending library.

42
00:05:23.429 --> 00:05:29.297
A book still under copyright can be borrowed there for an hour, free, with an Archive account.

43
00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:37.792
The FAQ answers common questions about God, the Bible, and the Christian life.

44
00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:41.485
Choose a question, and press Show the answer.

45
00:05:42.013 --> 00:05:49.655
The answers are written by Google's Gemini A.I., with every Scripture reference as a link, and some have a note from the site owner.

46
00:05:50.169 --> 00:05:53.588
The A.I. can make mistakes, and the page says so.

47
00:05:56.355 --> 00:06:03.250
Today, in the menu, has a Verse of the day: a well-known verse written over a photograph, new each time.

48
00:06:03.756 --> 00:06:07.342
Download the picture to share it, or press Show another.

49
00:06:09.615 --> 00:06:14.457
Devotional of the day does the same with a reading from one of the daily devotionals.

50
00:06:14.994 --> 00:06:24.136
Under the verse of the day, Make your own card: choose a verse and a background, and download it. When you are logged in, you can also send it to someone.

51
00:06:37.433 --> 00:06:40.304
With a free account, you can do even more.

52
00:06:43.204 --> 00:06:45.637
Everything works without an account.

53
00:06:46.137 --> 00:06:55.419
A free account adds your own notes and lists, daily devotional emails, a verse a day, text messages if you want them, and music playlists.

54
00:06:55.923 --> 00:07:07.386
Setting one up takes about a minute: your email address, and a password, typed twice. If you have no email address, a cell phone number will do instead, and you log in with it.

55
00:07:07.914 --> 00:07:10.590
Your name and phone number are optional.

56
00:07:16.829 --> 00:07:24.032
With a US or Canadian cell number, you choose how your messages come: by email, by text, or both.

57
00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:30.251
And tick, Send me a verse a day, to get a Bible verse each morning, at the time you choose.

58
00:07:33.025 --> 00:07:39.972
Once you are logged in, the round icon at the top right of every page is your menu. Point at it to open it.

59
00:07:40.476 --> 00:07:46.239
Account settings is where you add your picture, which then shows in that icon. Only you see it.

60
00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:54.468
You can also change your phone number, how your messages are sent, and your verse a day.

61
00:07:55.542 --> 00:07:59.853
To stop texts at any time, reply STOP to any text.

62
00:08:00.361 --> 00:08:06.647
You can change your password here, too, and at the bottom, close your account if you ever want to.

63
00:08:09.404 --> 00:08:15.109
You can write your own notes on any verse, commentary note, or devotional reading.

64
00:08:15.649 --> 00:08:20.062
Click a verse number, choose Notes, write your note, and save it.

65
00:08:29.712 --> 00:08:36.996
My Notes, in the same menu, keeps every note in one place, with a search, and a link back to each one.

66
00:08:39.704 --> 00:08:45.919
Any devotional can be emailed to you each day, and texted too, if you asked for texts.

67
00:08:46.442 --> 00:08:50.072
Choose the time and your time zone, and press the button.

68
00:08:52.057 --> 00:08:56.567
You can change the time, or stop the emails, whenever you like.

69
00:08:59.325 --> 00:09:05.518
On the media page, tick the songs you want, give the list a name, and save it as a playlist.

70
00:09:10.236 --> 00:09:14.093
Then press Play, and the songs play one after another.

71
00:09:17.827 --> 00:09:24.724
Press Edit to change a playlist: drag a song to a new place, remove one, or add others from a list.

72
00:09:35.757 --> 00:09:38.281
Every search can keep what you find.

73
00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:45.523
Tick the results you want, give the list a name, and press Save.

74
00:09:51.521 --> 00:09:58.632
My Lists keeps each list, with a link back to every entry, and Copy to notes turns a whole list into a note.

75
00:10:10.937 --> 00:10:17.350
Every card you make and keep, download, or send is saved on My cards, in your account menu.

76
00:10:20.061 --> 00:10:29.736
Edit a card to change its verse or its background, download it again, or send it: to someone on the site, by name, or to any email address.

77
00:10:32.524 --> 00:10:43.706
If you serve in a group at church, such as the greeters, My scheduled tasks, in your account menu, lists the days you are scheduled for, and whether each is confirmed.

78
00:10:44.247 --> 00:10:52.297
Add a task asks for one of your group's tasks, on a date you choose. It shows as not confirmed until your leader confirms it.

79
00:10:56.114 --> 00:11:00.353
Remove takes you off one, and your leader is emailed either way.

80
00:11:03.104 --> 00:11:07.821
Some features are turned on for each account by the site's administrator.

81
00:11:08.321 --> 00:11:11.519
To ask for them, use the Contact page.

82
00:11:16.024 --> 00:11:20.336
If the administrator allows it, you can share a list with everyone.

83
00:11:20.856 --> 00:11:23.529
Press, Share on Public lists.

84
00:11:24.056 --> 00:11:29.733
Public lists, under Members, shows the lists and playlists that members have shared.

85
00:11:30.831 --> 00:11:36.827
Anyone can read them and play a shared playlist, and a member can copy one to their own lists.

86
00:11:41.206 --> 00:11:47.979
With A.I. search, you describe what you are looking for in your own words, such as, forgiving someone who hurt me.

87
00:11:48.917 --> 00:11:54.608
The A.I. suggests verses from the Bibles on the site, each with the usual links.

88
00:11:57.353 --> 00:12:07.006
In the commentaries, the other books, the music, and Search Everything, A.I. search finds passages by their meaning, even when they use other words.

89
00:12:07.515 --> 00:12:13.104
A search for, the beatitudes, finds Matthew Henry's notes on the Sermon on the Mount.

90
00:12:18.019 --> 00:12:22.029
On the FAQ page, you can also ask your own question.

91
00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:26.449
Here we ask, how can I pray when I don't know what to say?

92
00:12:29.853 --> 00:12:33.736
The answer comes back with every Scripture reference as a link.

93
00:12:36.538 --> 00:12:41.013
Anyone can read Conversations, where members share with one another.

94
00:12:41.526 --> 00:12:45.813
Invited members can reply, and write posts of their own.

95
00:12:53.556 --> 00:13:04.452
Posts should not contain profanity, political messages, or ads; the posting policy says more. Tick, Email me replies, to hear about each new reply.

96
00:13:04.975 --> 00:13:13.466
Or choose one member under Send to, and only the two of you will see it. The first time, they are asked whether to accept posts from you.

97
00:13:13.972 --> 00:13:19.143
You can search every post and reply, and only you can change or delete your own.

98
00:13:21.873 --> 00:13:28.402
The Prayer Wall works the same way, for prayer requests and praises, kept apart from Conversations.

99
00:13:28.905 --> 00:13:33.761
Members share what they need prayer for, and others reply to say they are praying.

100
00:13:41.884 --> 00:13:53.908
Choose who sees each request: everyone, anonymously, only you, or everyone on the weekly prayer list. If you are in a group, you can send it to your group, or just to its leader.

101
00:14:02.727 --> 00:14:06.694
When a prayer is answered, its author can mark it, Answered.

102
00:14:07.228 --> 00:14:12.236
And anyone with an account can have the prayer list emailed to them, once a week.

103
00:14:15.104 --> 00:14:18.952
Invited members can also mark the maps for themselves.

104
00:14:19.485 --> 00:14:22.718
Drop a pin on a place, and write a note for it.

105
00:14:34.496 --> 00:14:41.183
Or trace a route, point by point, give it a name and a colour, and share it with other members if you like.

106
00:15:04.979 --> 00:15:09.452
Each map you mark is listed in My Notes, with a link back to it.

107
00:15:14.339 --> 00:15:19.962
And whenever you need it, the Help page is a full user guide, with pictures of every feature.

108
00:15:22.179 --> 00:15:27.831
This video is there, too, and the Privacy page says what the site keeps about you.

109
00:15:30.553 --> 00:15:32.225
Thank you for watching.

110
00:15:32.725 --> 00:15:37.570
Free Study Bible is free, with no ads, and nothing to install.
